  "2026-08-15T10:38:43.585Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for history-author-acknowledge,--all-actionable,dry-run,preview,zero selection,and the GitHub issue number found no item with this exact command-path defect. pm-h90s owns the completed acknowledgement feature,pm-jwmszf owns completed recovery discoverability,pm-tobi records the destructive-safety decision,and open pm-kexu covers update-many preview rather than this immutable-history command; all are linked as provenance,not duplicated or reopened."
  "2026-08-15T10:41:57.231Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence 2026-08-15: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1028#issuecomment-5301855572 points GitHub #1028 to this canonical PM item and summarizes the SDK-native preview/apply and zero-selection contract."
  "2026-08-15T10:56:12.274Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review evidence 2026-08-15: findings https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1031#discussion_r3789218618 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1031#discussion_r3789218619 were valid. The item now matches the live item-id:line/all_actionable grammar, defines a stable complete-set fingerprint with exact counts and ordering, requires fingerprint-bound apply with selection-drift rejection, and maps no_effect/partial_effect/usage/conflict/runtime outcomes to the existing 6/7/2/4/1 exit vocabulary."
body: "## Selector and preview contract\n\nCLI, SDK, and MCP preserve the existing exclusive selector grammar: repeated item-id:line event coordinates or all_actionable. The dry-run path and apply path use one SDK-native resolver. Preview returns selection.kind, canonical ordering by item_id then positive line, selected_count, omitted_count, a budget-bounded coordinates projection, and plan_fingerprint. The fingerprint is computed over the complete ordered coordinate set and the immutable source event hashes, so omitted coordinate rows do not weaken reproducibility.\n\n## Apply-transition contract\n\nApply must consume the preview fingerprint instead of trusting a second unconstrained all_actionable evaluation: CLI --plan-fingerprint, SDK planFingerprint, and MCP plan_fingerprint name the same field. Apply re-resolves under the same selector, compares the complete fingerprint, and returns CONFLICT exit 4 with a fresh-preview recovery if any actionable coordinate or source event changed. No acknowledgement is written on mismatch.\n\n## Outcome and exit contract\n\nZero matches and an explicit selection whose coordinates are all already acknowledged return outcome no_effect, acknowledged 0, mutated false, and exit 6. A mixed explicit selection with both newly actionable and already-acknowledged coordinates returns partial_effect and exit 7 with exact per-coordinate disposition rows. Malformed selectors return USAGE exit 2. Tracker or history corruption returns GENERIC_FAILURE exit 1. These stable outcomes replace the earlier unspecified strict-mode branch.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is specific to history-author-acknowledge. It complements the broader update-many preview work but does not depend on it and must not be folded into a generic destructive-command rewrite."
